Timecard App Sample
===================

This repo includes a lightweight web sample plus an iOS SwiftUI sample.

Features
--------
- Add time entries with start/end times and breaks
- Automatic daily hours plus weekly overtime estimate
- Per-employee totals
- Local storage persistence (browser localStorage or iOS UserDefaults)
- Export entries to CSV
- Sample data to try the UI quickly

Web Usage
---------
1. Open `index.html` in your browser.
2. Fill out the "Add time entry" form and submit.
3. Use the action buttons to export, clear, or load sample data.

iOS Usage (SwiftUI)
-------------------
1. Open Xcode and create a new iOS App project named `TimecardAppSample`.
2. Replace the generated `ContentView.swift` and `TimecardAppSampleApp.swift`
   with the files in `ios/TimecardAppSample`.
3. Add `TimeEntry.swift` and `TimeEntryStore.swift` to the project.
4. Build and run on a simulator or device.

Notes
-----
These are front-end-only samples intended for demos and learning. Data is
saved locally on the device (localStorage or UserDefaults).
